UPDATE companies SET description='Arkansas Steel Associates, LLC (ASA) was founded in 1989 as a joint venture between Yamato Kogyo and Sumitomo Corporation. The plant sits on 300 acres in Newport, Arkansas, in the northeastern part of the state.

ASA manufactures merchant bar quality (MBQ) billets, hot-rolled flat bars, and double-shoulder railroad tie plates. The facility produces tie plates to A.R.E.M.A. and customer specifications, with standard offerings covering rail sizes from 115RE to 140RE. Flat bars are produced in a variety of cross sections and lengths, all meeting Buy America requirements.

The company serves the railroad industry, supplying tie plates to customers that range from small contractors to Class 1 railroads across North America.

