UPDATE companies SET description='Arkansaw Woodworking operates from Fayetteville, Arkansas, serving the Northwest Arkansas region.

The company produces custom furniture and home decor pieces for homes, offices, and outdoor spaces. Its services include lumber milling, with a sawmill capable of processing logs up to 36 inches wide and 16 feet long, as well as furniture restoration for heirloom pieces. The workshop handles projects from raw log processing through final assembly and finishing.

Clients range from homeowners seeking one-of-a-kind dining tables, shelving, and decorative accents to businesses needing tailored office furnishings and outdoor installations. The shop works directly with customers to translate design ideas into finished pieces, covering projects from statement furniture to decorative accents.

Arkansaw Woodworking emphasizes handcrafted quality, blending traditional woodworking techniques with modern innovation. The team collaborates closely with each client to ensure every detail matches their vision, aiming to create pieces built to last generations. This client-centered approach drives the company''s reputation for tailored craftsmanship.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom furniture manufacturing", "Home decor fabrication", "Lumber milling (logs up to 36 in wide, 16 ft long)", "Furniture restoration"], "industries": ["Residential furniture", "Office furniture", "Outdoor furniture"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Sawmill (up to 36 in wide, 16 ft long)"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Handcrafted custom furniture and home decor", "Sawmill capacity for logs up to 36 inches wide and 16 feet long", "Furniture restoration and heirloom repair", "Direct collaboration with clients to tailor each piece", "Blends traditional techniques with modern innovation"], "facts_used": ["Location: Fayetteville, AR -> db", "Services: custom furniture, home decor, lumber milling, furniture restoration -> /", "Sawmill capacity: logs up to 36in wide, 16ft long -> /", "Service area: Northwest Arkansas -> /", "Handcrafted focus and traditional/modern blend -> /", "Client collaboration and tailored pieces -> /", "Restoration of heirloom furniture -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Our core service is custom furniture and home decor pieces for home & office spaces.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='arkansaw-woodworking' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Arrow Sheet Metal Works, Inc. operates from Tampa, Florida, where it has been located since 1964. The business was founded in 1952 by Fred Philippus and remains family-owned; his son Bob Philippus and his wife have held ownership since 1985. Bob, who has been involved since 1965, serves as vice president.

The company provides custom sheet metal fabrication, working with stainless steel, aluminum, steel, galvanized steel, brass, and copper. Its shop performs welding, grinding, polishing, shearing, and bending of materials up to 1/2 inch thick, as well as pipe bending up to 2 inches in diameter. Typical output includes countertops, handrails, brackets, platforms, frames, stands, kitchen hood shells, shelving, racks, panels, cabinets, truck boxes, light brackets, and transition fittings. Field installation and portable welding services are also offered, and local delivery is handled with company-owned pickup trucks and a flatbed.

Arrow serves both commercial and residential customers throughout the Tampa Bay area.

