UPDATE companies SET description='Atlas Metal Works LLC operates from South Windsor, Connecticut, as a CT DAS Certified Small Business Enterprise. The company runs a custom metal fabrication house serving the commercial market, though its founding year and founders are not publicly disclosed.

The shop provides end-to-end fabrication from design through finished parts, including laser cutting, high-definition plasma cutting, shearing, press-brake forming, CNC punching, pipe rolling and bending, polishing, sawing, and multiple welding processes (MIG, TIG, flux-core, spot, stud, and aluminum MIG). Key equipment includes a BLM LS5 12 kW plate laser cutting 5-by-10-foot plates up to one inch thick, a Vectis UR20 cobot welder with 48-inch reach, two AccurPress brakes (320-ton by 12-foot and 175-ton by 10-foot), an AccurShear with 1/4-inch by 12-foot capacity, a 55-ton Euromac CNC punch, a Timesaver 8-inch stainless polisher, Hypertherm and Thermadyne high-definition plasma systems, and a Marvel 18-inch automated saw. The company also stocks and sells raw sheet, plate, angle, and channel cut to size.

Customers span OEM manufacturers, general contractors, construction firms, and other fabrication houses that need supplemental capacity. Work ranges from commercial and residential projects to industrial applications, with the shop handling everything from gauge sheet to heavy plate in stainless steel, aluminum, carbon steel, galvanized, brass, and copper.

Atlas Metal Works positions itself as a gap-filler for manufacturers lacking in-house shearing, bending, laser cutting, welding, or hole-punching capacity. It accepts customer design files in AutoCAD, FastCAM, or FastSHAPES formats and can also create designs in-house, aiming to deliver accurate parts on schedule for both large and small projects.', certifications=ARRAY['CT DAS Certified Small Business Enterprise']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Laser cutting", "High-definition plasma cutting", "Shearing", "Press brake forming", "CNC punching", "Pipe rolling", "Pipe bending", "Stainless steel polishing", "Automated sawing", "MIG welding", "TIG welding", "Flux-core welding", "Spot welding", "Stud welding", "Aluminum MIG welding", "Design services (AutoCAD, FastCAM, FastSHAPES)", "Raw material sales (cut-to-size)", "Custom fabrication", "Installation"], "industries": ["Commercial", "Residential", "Industrial", "OEM manufacturing", "General contracting", "Construction"], "materials": ["Stainless steel", "Aluminum", "Steel", "Galvanized sheet metal", "Brass", "Copper"], "equipment": ["BLM LS5 12kw Plate Laser", "Vectis Technologies UR20 Cobot Welder", "AccurPress 320 ton x 12''", "AccurPress 175 ton x 10''", "AccurShear 1/4\" x 12''", "Euromac CNC Punch 55 Ton", "Timesaver Stainless Steel Polisher 8\" Wide", "Hypertherm 260 Amp High Definition Plasma", "Thermadyne 300 Amp High Definition Plasma", "Saw Marvel 18\" Automated"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["CT DAS Certified Small Business Enterprise", "Complete projects from design to finished product", "Accepts AutoCAD, FastCAM, and FastSHAPES design files", "Laser cutting up to 1-inch thick plate on 5'' x 10'' bed", "Cobot welding with 48-inch reach"], "facts_used": ["South Windsor, Connecticut headquarters -> db", "CT DAS Certified Small Business Enterprise -> /", "Custom metal fabrication house serving commercial market -> /", "Serves OEM manufacturers, general contractors, const