UPDATE companies SET description='Averra Packaging is based in West Valley City, Utah. The company was founded in 2013, though its thermoforming roots trace back to a garage operation started in 1989. Tim Neiman serves as CEO, a team that includes veterans of medical device manufacturing and packaging.

The company designs and manufactures custom sterile packaging for medical devices, as well as consumer packaging. Its 40,000-square-foot facility operates a Class 8 cleanroom and is cGMP compliant, with ISO 13485:2016 and ISO 9001:2015 certifications. Processes include thermoforming, in-house prototyping, bridge tooling for production-equivalent samples, and full-scale production supported by an internal machine shop that builds and maintains tooling. The equipment fleet handles volumes ranging from hundreds of parts to tens of millions annually.

Averra serves medical device manufacturers, healthcare companies, and consumer goods brands. Its healthcare portfolio includes custom trays, lids, and fulfillment services, with the company also acting as manufacturer of record for clients seeking a single point of accountability. Consumer packaging projects focus on shelf-impact design combined with functional performance.

The company emphasizes sustainable practices, reporting that 75 percent of its materials come from recycled content, one million pounds of post-production waste are recycled each year, and 96 percent of its products are recyclable. Averra positions itself as a development partner rather than a vendor, offering manufacturer-of-record capabilities to streamline quality systems and documentation for medical device launches.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 13485:2016','ISO 9001:2015','cGMP compliant','Class 8 cleanroom']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom sterile packaging design", "Thermoforming", "In-house prototyping", "Bridge Tooling\u2122", "In-house tooling design and machining", "Production thermoforming", "Class 8 cleanroom manufacturing", "cGMP compliance", "Manufacturer-of-record services", "Fulfillment services", "Consumer packaging design", "Design & development", "Sustainable packaging solutions"], "industries": ["Medical devices", "Healthcare", "Consumer goods"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "Hundreds to tens of millions of parts", "lead_time": "Prototyping in days; production tooling 30-60 business days", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["In-house prototyping delivers true thermoformed samples in days", "Bridge Tooling\u2122 provides production-equivalent parts for verification and ship testing", "In-house machine shop designs and builds tooling for repeatable, high-quality production", "Class 8 cleanroom and cGMP-compliant manufacturing for sterile medical packaging", "Manufacturer-of-record services consolidate packaging and regulatory accountability", "Sustainable operations: 75% recycled material content, 1M lbs waste recycled annually, 96% product recyclability"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2013 -> db", "Headquarters West Valley City, Utah -> db", "Thermoforming roots in garage 1989 -> /about", "40,000 sq-ft facility -> /about", "Class 8 cleanroom -> /capabilities", "cGMP compliant -> /capabilities", "ISO 13485:2016 and ISO 9001:2015 certified -> /capabilities", "In-house prototyping in days -> /capabilities", "Bridge Tooling\u2122 for production-equivalent parts -> /capabilities", "In-house machine shop for tooling -> /capabilities", "Manufacturer-of-record capabilities -> /capabilities", "Volumes from hundreds to tens of millions -> /about", "75% materials from recycled content -> /about", "1,000,000 lbs post-production waste recycled annually -> /about", "96% products recyclable -> /about", "Production tooling lead time 30-60 business days -> / (products list)", "Serves medical device, healthcare, consumer goods -> /, /about, /capabilities", "Custom trays, lids, fulfillment services -> /", "CEO Tim Neiman -> /about", "Team includes veterans of medical device manufacturing -> /about"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "we''ve evolved into a 40,000 sq-ft sterile healthcare packaging design & manufacturing facility", "founded_year": "2013", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='averra-packaging' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Azuma Foods International Inc. USA (AFI) was founded in 1990 and is headquartered in East Rutherford, New Jersey. The business was created to bring traditional Japanese food culture to a global audience by merging it with other culinary traditions.

AFI specializes in the import, processing, and distribution of Japanese-inspired seafood and specialty food products. Its product lines include tobikko (flying fish roe), masago (capelin roe), dry toppings, seaweed salad, calamari salad, and a range of sushi-grade, appetizer, fry-and-grill, and plant-based items. The company operates an in-house laboratory equipped for pathogen testing using PCR thermal cyclers, ELISA assays, and culture methods, and it develops new products through its R&D team. All foreign suppliers must provide HACCP plans and certificates of compliance, and AFI manages allergen control, gluten testing, and FSVP programs.

AFI was founded on the principle of assimilating food cultures, aiming to introduce traditional Japanese flavors to global markets through innovative product development. The company emphasizes rigorous food safety, with HACCP and SQF certifications, third-party audits, and a comprehensive quality management system that covers everything from supplier verification to in-house microbial testing.', certifications=ARRAY['HACCP','SQF']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Tobikko production", "Masago production", "Dry toppings manufacturing", "Seaweed salad processing", "Calamari salad processing", "New product development", "HACCP plan development and verification", "In-house microbial testing (PCR, ELISA, culture methods)", "Allergen control program", "Gluten testing", "FSVP compliance", "Supplier certification management"], "industries": ["Food Service"], "materials": ["Flying fish roe (tobikko)", "Capelin roe (masago)", "Ogo seaweed", "Calamari", "Tofu", "Shrimp"], "equipment": ["PCR thermal cyclers", "ELISA testing equipment", "Culture method testing equipment"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["HACCP and SQF certified quality management system", "In-house pathogen testing laboratory with PCR and ELISA capabilities", "Full supplier verification including HACCP plan review and certificates of compliance", "Allergen control, gluten testing, and FSVP program", "Award-winning sustainable, vegetarian-friendly product development (e.g., Island Style Marinated Ogo Seaweed)"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1990, headquartered East Rutherford, NJ -> db", "Mission: assimilation of food culture -> /", "Product lines: tobikko, masago, dry toppings, seaweed salad, calamari salad, sushi grade, appetizer, fry & grill, plant based -> /", "In-house laboratory with PCR thermal cyclers, ELISA testing, culture methods -> /quality", "HACCP and SQF certifications -> db, /quality", "Supplier HACCP plan verification and certificates of compliance -> /quality", "Allergen program, gluten testing, FSVP program -> /quality", "Serves food service industry -> db", "Menu catalog and recipe ideas for chefs -> /", "Award finalist for Island Style Marinated Ogo Seaweed -> /", "Sustainable, vegetarian-friendly, no added color -> /", "Processed at our facility -> /quality"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "processed at our facility", "founded_year": "1990", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='azuma-foods-international-inc-usa' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='B&B Molding Inc operates from Brandon, South Dakota, as a family-owned and operated rotational molding specialist. The company does not disclose its founding year, but describes itself as having years of combined experience in precision molding.

The shop focuses on rotational molding to produce durable, cost-effective plastic parts for a range of industries. Beyond molding, it offers hassle-free drop shipping, pallet wrapping, and assembly services, handling production, packaging, and shipping so customers can avoid inventory overhead. The team also works with custom molds and ready-to-ship products, emphasizing flexibility and quick turnaround times.

While the company serves a variety of industries, it does not name specific sectors or customers in its public materials. Its services are positioned for businesses seeking plastic components without the burden of warehousing or logistics.

B&B Molding states that quality is its top priority, with careful monitoring from design through production. The family-run structure is cited as a source of integrity, honesty, and teamwork, and the company highlights its commitment to customer satisfaction and cost-effective solutions.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Rotational molding", "Drop shipping", "Pallet wrapping", "Assembly", "Custom mold design"], "industries": [], "materials": ["Plastic"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Hassle-free drop shipping with no upfront inventory costs", "Pallet wrapping to protect products during transit", "Assembly services for ready-to-use components", "Family-owned operation emphasizing integrity and teamwork", "Quality monitored at every stage from design to production"], "facts_used": ["Located in Brandon, South Dakota -> db", "Family owned and operated -> homepage", "Specializes in rotational molding -> homepage", "Offers drop shipping, pallet wrapping, and assembly services -> homepage", "Emphasizes quality control and customer satisfaction -> homepage", "Provides custom molds and ready-to-ship products -> homepage"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "B & B Molding specializes in rotational molding, producing durable, cost-effective plastic products for a variety of industries.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='b-b-molding-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='BAK Food Equipment is headquartered in Burr Ridge, Illinois. The company was founded by John Bobak, who built on his success scaling a sausage operation to establish a business focused on helping other food processors achieve their production goals. While the exact founding year is not publicly disclosed, the company emphasizes decades of hands-on experience in the food manufacturing industry.

The company designs and manufactures a range of food processing equipment, including tumblers, brine injectors, smoke chambers, mixers, bowl cutters and emulsifiers, brine preparation systems, grinders, mixer grinders, washers, loaders, flakers, tenderizers, and dripping tunnels. It also provides custom automation solutions, integrating standalone machines into complete production lines. Engineering services cover initial consultation, design, specification, installation, and commissioning, with equipment featuring industrial-grade stainless steel construction and touchscreen controls for repeatable operation.

BAK serves a broad spectrum of food sectors: alternative proteins, baby food, bakery and confectionery, cheese and dairy, deli meats, fruits and nuts, ground meat and proteins, poultry, pet food, prepared foods, produce, pharmaceutical and chemical, red meat, sausage, seafood, smoked products, soups, sauces and oils, spices, and warehouse and industrial applications. Notable installations include a paddle mixer system across four plants for a snack stick producer, a spiral system for a large bacon processor that combined smoking, cooking, and chilling in a continuous line, and a bowl chopper upgrade for a farm-to-retail meat processor.

The company differentiates itself through fully customizable systems designed around each customer''s specific products, throughput targets, and space constraints. A one-year warranty on all parts and labor backs every installation, and a dedicated service team aims to minimize downtime. The founder''s background in sausage processing informs an approach that prioritizes food safety, product consistency, and long-term partnership from consultation through ongoing maintenance.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Food processing equipment design and manufacturing", "Custom automation solutions", "Production line integration", "Equipment installation and commissioning", "Preventive maintenance and service", "Spare parts supply", "Tumbling", "Brine injection", "Smoking and cooking (smoke chambers)", "Mixing and blending", "Bowl cutting/emulsifying", "Brine preparation", "Grinding", "Washing", "Loading systems", "Flaking, tenderizing, dripping tunnels", "Touchscreen controls programming", "Stainless steel fabrication", "Food safety compliance engineering"], "industries": ["Alternative Proteins", "Baby Food", "Bakery & Confectionary", "Cheese & Dairy", "Deli Meats", "Fruits & Nuts", "Ground Meat and Proteins", "Poultry", "Pet Food", "Prepared Food", "Produce", "Pharmaceutical/Chemical", "Red Meat", "Sausage", "Seafood", "Smoked Products", "Soup, Sauce, and Oil", "Spices", "Warehouse & Industrial"], "materials": ["Stainless steel"], "equipment": ["Tumblers", "Brine Injectors", "Smoke Chambers & Related Equipment", "Mixers", "Bowl Cutters/Emulsifiers", "Brine Preparation", "Grinders", "Mixer Grinder", "Washers", "Loaders", "Flakers, Tenderizers & Dripping Tunnels", "Custom Automation Solution"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Full one-year warranty on all parts and labor", "Customizable systems designed around specific products, throughput targets, and space constraints", "Decades of hands-on food processing experience from founder who scaled a sausage operation", "In-depth consultation through design, installation, and ongoing maintenance", "Modular components and scalable system architectures for future expansion"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters: Burr Ridge, IL -> db", "Founder: John Bobak -> pages[''/'']", "Equipment list: Tumblers, Brine Injectors, Smoke Chambers, Mixers, Bowl Cutters/Emulsifiers, Brine Preparation, Grinders, Mixer Grinder, Washers, Loaders, Flakers, Tenderizers & Dripping Tunnels, Custom Automation Solution -> pages[''/'']", "Industries served: Alternative Proteins, Baby Food, Bakery & Confectionary, Cheese & Dairy, Deli Meats, Fruits & Nuts, Ground Meat and Proteins, Poultry, Pet Food, Prepared Food, Produce, Pharmaceutical/Chemical, Red Meat, Sausage, Seafood, Smoked Products, Soup Sauce and Oil, Spices, Warehouse & Industrial -> pages[''/'']", "Case studies: Snack Stick Producer (four plants), Large Bacon Producer (spiral system), Farm-to-Retail Meat Processor (bowl chopper) -> pages[''/'']", "Warranty: one-year on all parts and labor -> pages[''/'']", "Company description: specializes in tailored food production lines with modular components and scalable architectures -> db", "LinkedIn URL -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "BAK Food Equipment specializes in tailored food production lines that are designed with expansion and adaptability in mind.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/bakfoodequipment/"], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='bak-food-equipment' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='BBG Incorporated was founded in 1988 in Chesapeake, Virginia, as an engineering firm focused on electronic design and manufacturing for commercial and military sectors. The company has grown to provide end-to-end solutions from concept through production, serving both domestic and international markets.

BBG offers a full suite of in-house capabilities including PCB design and fabrication (Mil-Spec to IPC, RoHS compliant), PCB layout, manufacturing from prototype to high-volume runs, and rigorous testing and inspection. Its engineering services span hardware and software design, firmware development for ARM/MCU and RTOS platforms, HMI/GUI design, FPGA/CPLD development (VHDL/Verilog), data conversion for legacy and modern systems, and systems integration. The firm also provides complete assembly and production—mechanical enclosures, wire harnessing, and system integration—along with shipboard installation and modernization services for U.S. and foreign naval platforms.

The company primarily serves defense, aerospace, and military customers, with a client list that includes major primes such as Northrop Grumman, BAE Systems, Lockheed Martin, and General Dynamics. It also supports commercial sector projects requiring ruggedized electronics, test equipment, and Ethernet-based networking products.

BBG emphasizes its USA-based manufacturing, end-to-end in-house control, and cutting-edge automated testing and visual inspection systems as key differentiators. The firm was built to solve complex engineering challenges, modernize legacy systems, and deliver cost-effective, high-performance solutions with on-time delivery.', certifications=ARRAY['RoHS']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["PCB design & fabrication (Mil-Spec, IPC, RoHS)", "PCB layout & design", "PCB manufacturing (prototyping to high-volume)", "PCB testing & inspection", "Data conversion (legacy to modern systems)", "Hardware design & engineering", "Software engineering (firmware, RTOS, HMI/GUI, embedded systems, networking, wireless)", "FPGA/CPLD design (VHDL/Verilog)", "Product design & development (concept to prototyping)", "Systems integration (legacy and modern hardware)", "Assembly & production (mechanical enclosures, wire harnessing, system integration)", "Quality control (automated testing, visual inspection)", "Shipboard installation & integration", "Shipboard system modernization", "Military-grade compliance", "Legacy product modernization", "Signal conversion", "Edge computing solutions", "Rugged solutions manufacturing", "Test equipment manufacturing", "Ethernet products manufacturing"], "industries": ["Defense", "Aerospace", "Military", "Commercial"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "Prototype to high-volume production", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["USA-based manufacturing from prototype to high-volume production", "In-house PCB design, fabrication, assembly, and test under one roof", "Expertise in military/aerospace data conversion and legacy system modernization", "Shipboard installation and integration for U.S. and foreign naval systems", "Established partnerships with top defense primes (Northrop Grumman, BAE, Lockheed Martin, General Dynamics)"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1988 in Chesapeake, Virginia -> /about", "Electronic design and manufacturing 