UPDATE companies SET description='Morrow, originally from Nashville, Tennessee, transitioned from a career as a professional bass trombonist to woodworking, establishing the shop in Katonah while primarily serving clients in New York City.

The company produces custom furniture, fixtures, and installations on a commissioned basis, handling each project from design through build, finishing, delivery, and installation. The shop works with solid woods such as white oak, plywood, and reclaimed or locally recycled lumber, emphasizing hand-selected materials for each piece.

Projects range from individual furniture pieces to larger built-in installations, all managed by Morrow from concept to completion.

Morrow founded the business after leaving the music industry, a move he describes as a "BIG SIN" in his former field. The operation distinguishes itself by keeping the entire process under one maker, ensuring material traceability and a direct relationship between the craftsman and the client.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom furniture making", "Fixture fabrication", "Installation services", "Design consultation", "Wood finishing", "Material selection and sourcing", "Commissioned project management", "Delivery and installation"], "industries": [], "materials": ["White oak", "Plywood", "Reclaimed wood", "Locally recycled wood"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Single maker handles design, build, finish, delivery, and installation", "Hand-selected materials including locally recycled and reclaimed wood", "Custom commissions from concept to completion", "Built-to-order in New York"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2018 by Jeremy Morrow -> /about", "Founder from Nashville, TN, now in New York -> /about", "Shop located in Katonah, work delivered to NYC -> /about", "Produces custom furniture, fixtures, installations built-to-order -> /", "Commissioned works from design to build -> /", "Uses white oak, plywood, reclaimed/recycled wood -> /about", "Single-person control from design through installation -> /about", "Founder previously professional musician (bass trombone) -> /about", "Headquarters in Brooklyn, NY -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "custom furniture, fixtures, and installations built-to-order in new york", "founded_year": "2018", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='big-sin-wood' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='BK Industries operates from Meridian, Idaho, in the Treasure Valley region. The shop is owned and operated by Brian Krah, a lifelong automotive enthusiast who has worked professionally in the industry for nearly two decades. Before establishing BK Industries, Krah owned and ran an automotive repair and performance shop in eastern Idaho and served as a Honda technician at a dealership, building deep expertise with Japanese vehicles.

The business functions as a full-service automotive shop, offering repair, preventive maintenance, and performance upgrades. While its core focus is Japanese makes, the team also services domestic and other import vehicles. The shop sources and installs parts for a range of needs, from routine maintenance to custom performance builds.

BK Industries serves individual vehicle owners and automotive enthusiasts throughout the Treasure Valley. Its customer base includes drivers of Japanese brands such as Honda, as well as domestic and other import models. The shop’s reputation draws clients seeking specialized knowledge of Japanese platforms alongside general automotive repair.

Krah’s involvement in the enthusiast community underscores the shop’s credibility; in 2000 his highly customized 1999 Honda Civic Coupe was selected for display at the SEMA show in Las Vegas, representing several well-known aftermarket brands. That recognition reflects the technical depth and passion that BK Industries brings to every vehicle it services.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Automotive repair", "Preventive maintenance", "Performance tuning", "Parts sourcing and installation", "Japanese vehicle specialization", "Domestic and import vehicle service"], "industries": ["Automotive service", "Automotive aftermarket"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Specializes in Japanese vehicle service and performance", "Experience with domestic and import vehicles", "Owner Brian Krah has nearly 20 years professional automotive experience", "SEMA 2000 display vehicle representing multiple aftermarket brands"], "facts_used": ["Location: Meridian, Idaho -> db", "Owner: Brian Krah -> /about-us", "Owner''s professional experience: nearly 20 years -> /about-us", "Previous shop in eastern Idaho -> /about-us", "Honda technician at dealership -> /about-us", "SEMA 2000 display -> /about-us", "Specializes in Japanese cars -> /", "Experience with domestic and imports -> /", "Services: service, maintenance, performance -> /", "Strives to provide best parts and services -> /"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Idaho''s premier service, maintenance and performance shop.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='bk-industries-japanese-car-specialist' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='BSU Electronics operates from Austin, Texas, where it has manufactured printed circuit board assemblies since relocating from its founding location in Ithaca, New York. The company was established in 1989 and today is led by Chief Executive Officer Leyla Sudbury and Executive Chairman Andrew Cousin, with Ahmad Chamseddine serving as senior advisor. What began as a PCB assembly shop has grown into a full-service electronics contract manufacturer serving customers from startup phase through global production.

The company provides end-to-end electronics manufacturing including rigid, flex, and rigid‑flex PCB assembly using surface‑mount, through‑hole, and press‑fit processes. Its facility handles box‑build and electromechanical system integration, custom cable and wire harness assembly (including fiber optic, RF, coax, and high‑gauge overmolded designs), conformal coating, and software/firmware programming. Testing capabilities span flying‑probe, 5D X‑ray, 3D automated optical inspection, in‑line solder paste inspection, functional test, boundary scan, ionic contamination, temperature cycling, and high‑potential verification. All work is performed to IPC‑A‑610, IPC J‑STD‑001, and IPC/WHMA‑A‑620 standards with full traceability under ITAR registration.

BSU serves aerospace programs with mission‑critical avionics, communication boards, and aircraft spares; defense customers with manned and unmanned system components; semiconductor equipment builders including wafer‑fabrication platforms; medical technology firms; transportation projects ranging from roller coasters and monorails to autonomous and electric vehicles; energy sector subassemblies for generation, storage, and AI data‑center power; and broader industrial automation, sensor, and instrumentation electronics. Long‑term relationships include a 30‑year safety‑equipment client and multiple multi‑decade aerospace and defense accounts supplying the U.S. government.

The company emphasizes engineer‑led sourcing and design‑for‑X collaboration so that manufacturability issues surface during build rather than qualification. It advertises flexible lead times — under 24‑hour turnaround when components are on hand, three‑day new‑quote response, and one‑day rush for repeat customers — backed by direct, proactive engineering engagement throughout each project.', certifications=ARRAY['ITAR registered','RoHS compliant','IPC-A-610','IPC J-STD-001','IPC/WHMA-A-620']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["PCB assembly (SMT, through-hole, press-fit)", "Box build & system integration", "Cable & wire harness assembly", "Conformal coating", "Design-for-X services (DFM, DFA, DFT, DFC, DFAv)", "Debug & rework", "BGA re-ball", "Component removal & replacement", "Flying probe testing", "5D X-ray inspection", "Automated optical inspection (AOI)", "3D AOI", "Solder paste inspection (SPI) in-line", "Functional testing", "Visual inspection", "Ionic contamination testing", "Temperature cycling", "High potential (hipot) testing", "Boundary scan testing", "Software programming & integration", "Device programming", "Firmware download", "Turnkey & consigned sourcing", "Obsolete component sourcing", "Domestic ITAR-compliant sourcing"], "industries": ["Aerospace", "Defense", "Semiconductor", "Medical technology", "Transportation", "Energy", "Industrial"], "materials": ["Rigid PCB", "Flex PCB", "Rigid-flex PCB", "Multi-layer PCB", "Controlled impedance PCB", "High frequency PCB", "Lead-free solder (RoHS)", "No-clean solder", "Clean solder", "Fiber optic cable", "RF cable", "Power cable", "Shielded cable", "Twisted pair cable", "Coaxial cable", "Heavy gauge wire"], "equipment": ["5D X-Ray", "Flying probe", "AOI / 3D AOI", "SPI In-Line", "Automatic cable eye testing", "Jet-Paste", "Programmable selective soldering", "Wave soldering", "Reflow"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "<24-hour turnaround when parts are in hand, 3 business days for new quotes, 1-day rush turnaround for existing customers with parts available", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Engineer-led sourcing and design review to catch issues before qualification", "Under 24-hour turnaround when parts are in hand", "Three-business-day response for new quotes", "One-day rush turnaround for existing customers with parts available", "ITAR-registered U.S. manufacturer with full traceability to IPC-A-610 and IPC J-STD-001"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1989 in Ithaca, now manufacturing in Austin -> /about-us", "CEO Leyla Sudbury, Executive Chairman Andrew Cousin, Senior Advisor Ahmad Chamseddine -> /about-us", "PCB types: rigid, flex, rigid-flex, multi-layer, controlled impedance, high frequency -> /", "Sourcing: turnkey, consigned, cut tape, loose reels, obsolete, domestic ITAR-compliant -> /", "Assembly: SMT, through-hole, press-fit, V-score, mouse-bites, mechanical routing -> /", "Soldering: jet-paste, stencil printing, reflow, wave, programmable selective soldering, clean, no clean -> /", "Repair: debug, rework, BGA re-ball, component removal and replacement -> /", "Testing: flying probe, 5D X-ray, AOI, SPI in-line, functional, visual, ionic contamination, temperature cycling, high potential, boundary scan, 3D AOI -> /", "Design-for-X: quality, cost, availability, manufacturability, fixtures and test jigs -> /", "Add-ons: box build, conformal coating, system integration, software programming and integration -> /", "Cables/harnesses: internal, external, RF, shielded, unshielded, coax, flex, twisted pair -> /", "Industries: semiconductor, aerospace, defense, transportation, energy, broader industrial -> /", "Medical mentioned in about page -> /about-us", "ITAR registered, IPC-A-610, IPC J-STD-001, IPC/WHMA-A-620 -> /capabilities", "Lead times: <24hr when parts in hand, 3 days new quotes, 1 day rush for existing -> /"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We are a full-service partner for printed circuit board assembly (PCBA), box builds, cabling and electronics contract manufacturing (ECM).", "founded_year": "1989", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": ["ITAR registered"], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='bsu-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='BT Fab LLC was established in 2005 in Reno, Nevada, and now operates from Sparks in the Reno–Tahoe area. The business was founded on a straightforward premise: deliver quality sheet metal products on time and at a fair price.

The shop provides a full range of sheet metal fabrication services, including plasma cutting, shearing (10‑foot, 10‑gauge capacity), braking (10‑foot, 10‑gauge), roto‑die forming, rolling, roll forming, welding, notching, beading, and turning. Its equipment roster features a Lockformer plasma cutting system, shears, brakes, a roll former, insulation equipment, hand brakes, and assorted welding and forming machines.

BT Fab serves residential, commercial, and industrial customers. Typical projects include HVAC duct work, flashing, custom pans, and fabrication in copper and stainless steel. The firm describes its clientele as ranging from small businesses and individual homeowners to larger industrial enterprises.

