UPDATE companies SET description='BTL Liners, based in Prineville, Oregon, traces its roots to 1981 when Ron Perlatti founded Bend Tarp and Liner in Bend. The company began installing pond liners in the mid-1980s and partnered with a Japanese firm to develop the first heavyweight reinforced polyethylene liners. Ownership passed to Perlatti''s son Brad and his wife Jan in 1997, and the operation moved to its current 84,000-square-foot facility in Prineville in 2007, adopting the BTL Liners name. In 2021, their daughter Chelsea and her husband Travis Wilcox took over, continuing the third-generation family ownership.

The company manufactures custom geomembrane liners, covers, and tarps from reinforced polyethylene (RPE), reinforced polypropylene (RPP), and low-density polyethylene (LDPE). Its purpose-built fabrication plant houses welding and prefabrication equipment capable of producing single panels up to 150,000 square feet. A team of 20-plus handles design, fabrication, and installation support offered worldwide, either on-site or remotely.

BTL serves agriculture, aquaponics, energy, mining, recreation, and environmental containment markets. Projects include cable wake-board parks in California and Ohio, golf-course ponds in Oregon, greenhouse covers worldwide, a 40-acre irrigation reservoir in the western U.S., frac-tank insulated covers, a coal-mine liner in British Columbia, and custom truck and boat tarps.

The firm emphasizes its 45-year track record, 280-plus years of combined staff experience, and a guarantee of 100% reliability with after-project support. It positions its RPE/RPP materials as stronger, lighter, and more UV-resistant alternatives to traditional HDPE, PVC, or EPDM liners.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom geomembrane liner fabrication", "Reinforced polyethylene (RPE) liner manufacturing", "Reinforced polypropylene (RPP) liner manufacturing", "Low density polyethylene (LDPE) liner manufacturing", "Welding and fabrication of geomembranes", "Prefabricated panel production (up to 150,000 sq ft)", "Installation assistance (onsite and remote)", "Custom tarp and cover manufacturing", "Greenhouse cover manufacturing", "Design of containment systems", "Custom truck and boat tarp fabrication", "Light deprivation greenhouse cover manufacturing"], "industries": ["Agriculture", "Aquaponics", "Energy", "Hydroponics", "Greenhouse Light Deprivation", "Water Gardens", "Farm Ponds", "Greenhouses", "Golf Course Pond", "Golf Course Water Feature", "Landfill Cover", "Irrigation", "Irrigation Pond", "Irrigation Canal", "Cable Wake Board Parks", "Frac Tank", "Coal Mine", "Ice Skating", "Truck and Boat Tarps"], "materials": ["Reinforced polyethylene (RPE)", "Reinforced polypropylene (RPP)", "Low density polyethylene (LDPE)"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Largest single panels in the industry up to 150,000 sq ft", "84,000 sq ft purpose-built fabrication facility", "Installation assistance worldwide (onsite or remote)", "45 years in business (since 1981)", "Over 280 years of combined industry experience among staff"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1981 by Ron Perlatti -> /about-us", "Headquarters Prineville, Oregon -> db and /about-us", "84,000 sq ft facility since 2007 -> /about-us", "20+ employees -> /about-us", "Third-generation family-owned -> /about-us", "Manufactures RPE, RPP, LDPE liners -> /about-us", "Largest single panels up to 150,000 sq ft -> /", "Installation assistance worldwide -> /", "Industries: agriculture, aquaponics, energy, hydroponics, greenhouse, water gardens, farm ponds, golf course, landfill, irrigation, mining, recreation, transportation -> / and /about-us", "45 years in business -> /", "Over 280 years combined experience -> /about-us", "Market leader since 1981 -> /about-us", "100% reliability guarantee -> /about-us", "After-project support -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "At BTL, we manufacture custom liners made from reinforced polyethylene (RPE), reinforced polypropylene (RPP) and low density polyethylene (LDPE).", "founded_year": "1981", "employee_count": "20+", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='btl-liners' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='BY DESIGN Furniture & Interior Design operates from Clive, Iowa, a suburb of Des Moines. The business traces its roots to 1976 when Russell and Ruthann Clark encouraged their son Kevin and daughter-in-law Bonita to open Wood Stock Ltd., a store dedicated to unfinished wood furniture in Des Moines. The company remains a locally owned, family-run small business, now transitioning to new leadership under Spectrum Lighting with Jennifer Robinson managing operations.

The firm provides interior design services through degreed designers and retails a curated selection of residential and office furniture from brands such as American Leather, Four Hands, Norwalk Furniture, and BDI. Its showroom features a fabric wall with thousands of fabric and leather options, and dining tables configurable with wood, tile, stone, or glass tops. The company also offers a proprietary furniture protection program covering upholstery, leather, and case goods, and operates an online clearance channel.

BY DESIGN serves homeowners seeking full-room design and furnishing, as well as trade professionals through a dedicated "Outside Designers" program. Clients include residential customers in the Des Moines metro area and designers partnering on client projects. The company''s portfolio spans living, dining, bedroom, office, entertainment, and outdoor spaces.

