UPDATE companies SET description='Barku Plastics operates from Cleveland, Tennessee. The U.S. subsidiary was established in September 2003 by its German parent, Barku Kunststofftechnik GmbH, which traces its origins to 1 October 1977 when Egon Schumacher founded it as a subsidiary of LUBING Maschinenfabrik GmbH. The American operation began as an extension of that German expertise into the North American market.

The company produces precision plastic components through injection molding and profile extrusion. Its Cleveland plant runs more than 50 injection molding machines ranging from 32 to 1,100 tons, capable of two-component and insert molding, alongside over 10 extrusion lines that handle diameters up to 6 inches and profile widths up to 39 3/8 inches, including co-extrusion for multi-material profiles. Annual raw material throughput exceeds 14,000 tons, and the facility operates on a three-shift schedule.

Barku serves customers worldwide, working with mold builders on three continents and providing value-added assembly, engineering support, and custom mold development.

