UPDATE companies SET description='Base Power Company is headquartered in Austin, Texas, and was founded in 2023 by CEO Zach Dell and co‑founder Justin Lopas. Dell, a Texas native, was motivated by Winter Storm Uri’s widespread outages, while Lopas brought manufacturing experience from SpaceX and Anduril. The pair assembled a team with backgrounds in satellite constellations and early‑scale electric‑vehicle production to address rising electricity costs and grid reliability.

Its in‑house capabilities include battery pack assembly, UL‑certified testing, and virtual‑power‑plant grid‑services operation. As of the latest public figures, more than 30,000 homes have been equipped with Base hardware, which is rated for –22 °F to 122 °F, flash flooding, and submersion up to three feet.

Base serves residential homeowners across Texas and Illinois, with a concentration in Oncor territory, and positions its grid‑balancing battery network as a resource for utilities and grid operators. Customer testimonials cite installations in Waxahachie, Cypress, Houston, Arlington, Saginaw, and Pflugerville, and the company counts former NFL player JJ Watt as both an investor and a member.

