UPDATE companies SET description='Big Frog Custom T-Shirts & More operates a retail garment decorating boutique at 3505 West 41st Street in Sioux Falls, South Dakota. The Big Frog brand was established in 2008 by co-founders Leeward Bean, Tina Bacon-DeFrece, and Ron DeFrece in Clearwater, Florida, and has since grown to nearly 100 locations nationwide.

The shop specializes in direct-to-garment (DTG) printing with white ink, screen printing, embroidery, ultra print, direct-to-film, and vinyl decoration. It sources blank apparel from major brands such as Alternative, Bella+Canvas, Gildan, Nike, Puma, Adidas, and Travis Matthews. The facility offers free 15-minute design assistance and can produce orders ranging from a single piece to 500-plus units with no setup fees. Typical turnaround is 24 hours for in-stock garments, with same-day service possible for urgent requests.

The company serves local schools, clubs, associations, businesses, and charitable organizations, as well as individuals marking personal milestones such as birthdays, fun runs, team-building events, and sports spirit walks. Customers have included Secure Point Technologies, BH Haak, and numerous families and community groups.

Big Frog differentiates itself through a brand promise of free design help, 24-hour turnaround on in-stock items, no minimum orders or setup fees, friendly customer service, and a clean, green, hassle-free customization experience. The owners emphasize a community-first approach, positioning the shop as a local partner invested in helping customers stand out and succeed.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Direct-to-Garment (DTG) Printing", "Direct-to-Garment with White Ink (DTG-W)", "Screen Printing", "Embroidery", "Ultra Print", "Direct-to-Film Printing", "Vinyl Printing", "Free Design Assistance", "24-Hour Turnaround on In-Stock Garments", "No Minimum Orders", "No Setup Fees"], "industries": ["Education (schools)", "Non-profit / charitable organizations", "Corporate / business", "Sports teams", "Events", "Promotional products"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "1 to 500+ units", "lead_time": "24 hours for in-stock garments; same-day possible", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Free 15-minute design assistance", "24-hour turnaround on in-stock garments", "No minimum order quantities", "No setup fees", "Multiple decoration techniques (DTG, screen print, embroidery, ultra print, direct-to-film, vinyl)"], "facts_used": ["Location: 3505 W 41st St, Sioux Falls, SD 57106 -> /", "Founded 2008 by Leeward Bean, Tina Bacon-DeFrece, Ron DeFrece -> /about", "Sioux Falls franchise opened by Ryan & Ethan Corbin -> /", "Processes: DTG, DTG-W, screen printing, embroidery, ultra print, direct-to-film, vinyl -> /, /about", "Brands: Alternative, Bella+Canvas, Gildan, Nike, Puma, Adidas, Travis Matthews -> /about", "Free 15-minute design assistance -> /", "24-hour turnaround on in-stock garments -> /, /about", "No minimums, no setup fees -> /, /about", "Industries served: schools, clubs, associations, businesses, charitable organizations, events -> /", "Customer examples: Secure Point Technologies, BH Haak, etc. -> /", "Brand promise: free design help, 24-hour turnaround, no minimums/setup fees, friendly service, clean & green, hassle-free -> /about", "LinkedIn URL -> db"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Big Frog is a high-tech, light manufacturing retail garment decorating boutique.", "founded_year": "2008", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "No minimum order quantity", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/big-frog-custom-t-shirts/"], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='big-frog-custom-t-shirts-more' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Bio-Med Devices, Inc. is headquartered in Guilford, Connecticut. The company’s current ownership traces to 1984, when respiratory equipment sales representative Dean Bennett Jr. took out a second mortgage on his home to purchase the then-small business, which offered a single neonatal transport ventilator. The company remains family-owned, with Dean Bennett III now serving as CEO.

The company designs and manufactures a range of respiratory care products, including precision air/oxygen blenders, oxygen monitors, and full ventilator systems. Its catalog also encompasses circuits, hoses, stands, test lungs, and transport batteries, with numerous part numbers for neonatal, pediatric, and adult configurations. Bio-Med Devices emphasizes retrofittable designs that allow clinicians to upgrade existing blenders without replacing entire fleets, and it offers portable transport systems for critical care mobility.

Bio-Med Devices serves hospitals and clinical teams across neonatal, pediatric, and adult critical care settings. Its devices are used in environments ranging from ambulances and neonatal intensive care units (NICU) to pediatric ICUs and general adult ICUs. The company’s OxyMinder® Pro monitor provides real-time oxygen and pressure monitoring with adjustable alarms and a color touchscreen designed for low-light conditions.

The business was founded on the belief that clinicians deserve reliable, durable respiratory equipment backed by responsive support and real relationships. Leadership highlights more than five decades of engineering experience and a commitment to U.S. manufacturing, positioning the company as a partner that helps reduce capital costs while maintaining precision and safety in critical moments.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Design and manufacturing of respiratory care devices", "Air/oxygen blending", "Oxygen monitoring", "Ventilator system manufacturing", "Retrofitting of existing blenders", "Portable transport systems", "Circuit configuration and assembly", "Real-time oxygen and pressure monitoring", "Alarm system integration", "Touchscreen interface design"], "industries": ["Healthcare", "Respiratory care", "Neonatal care", "Pediatric care", "Adult critical care", "Emergency medical services"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Made in the USA", "Retrofittable designs reduce capital costs", "Real-time oxygen and pressure monitoring with adjustable alarms", "Color touchscreen for low-light NICU/PICU environments", "Family-owned with decades of engineering experience"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters: Guilford, CT -> db", "Family-owned -> /", "Dean Bennett Jr. purchased company in 1984 -> /", "Dean Bennett III is CEO -> /", "Designs and manufactures respiratory care devices -> /", "Products include air/oxygen blenders, oxygen monitors, ventilator systems -> /", "Serves neonatal, pediatric, adult care environments -> /", "Offers retrofitting for existing blenders -> /", "Made in the USA -> /", "OxyMinder Pro provides real-time monitoring with alarms and touchscreen -> /", "Commitment to reliable, durable equipment and responsive support -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "For over 50 years, Bio-Med Devices has been designing and manufacturing advanced respiratory care solutions trusted by clinicians worldwide.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='bio-med-devices-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Bixby Electric Inc is headquartered in Albuquerque, New Mexico, with operations spanning New Mexico, Colorado, Texas, Arizona, California, and Wyoming. The company has been active in the Southwest for over four decades, though a specific founding year is not publicly disclosed. Ownership structure and founder names are not detailed in available sources.

The firm provides electrical construction, testing, and maintenance services across commercial, industrial, and infrastructure sectors. Core capabilities include airfield lighting and NAVAID installation, roadway and traffic signal systems, intelligent transportation systems, and transmission and distribution work up to 115 kV in both underground and overhead configurations. Bixby also operates directional boring and vertical drilling crews, vacuum excavation for utility potholing, and a dedicated electrical testing division that performs infrared thermography, arc flash studies, and power quality analysis. The company maintains two service departments—one for electrical and one for transportation—and offers vac and sweeper truck rentals operated by its own personnel.

Customers include state and local transportation agencies, airports, utilities, healthcare facilities, water and wastewater plants, mining operations, and solar developers. Project examples cited by the company include the Bear Canyon Pedestrian Bridge lighting and the Montano Railrunner Station. Bixby emphasizes a "what we install, we maintain" approach, providing emergency repair services for both road and air traffic systems.

The company highlights its family-oriented culture, participation in the Northern New Mexico Independent Electrical Contractors Association apprenticeship program, and MSHA-certified technicians for mine and pit work as differentiators.', certifications=ARRAY['MSHA certifications']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Electrical construction", "Electrical testing and commissioning", "Airfield lighting and NAVAID installation and maintenance", "Roadway lighting, traffic signals, and intelligent transportation systems", "Transmission and distribution up to 115 kV (underground and overhead)", "Directional boring and horizontal directional drilling", "Vertical drilling (pressure digger up to 54\" diameter, 20'' deep)", "Vacuum excavation and potholing", "Infrared thermography and ultrasonic testing", "Arc flash studies and power quality analysis", "Lighting retrofits", "Solar energy installations", "Medium voltage installations", "Weigh-in-motion (WIM) systems", "High mast lighting", "Emergency repair services", "Vac truck rental (hydro-excavation)", "Sweeper truck rental"], "industries": ["Transportation (airfield, roadway)", "Industrial", "Commercial", "Residential", "Government", "Utilities", "Healthcare", "Water and wastewater", "Mining", "Solar energy"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Sterling LT9500 Vac Truck", "International 4300 Elgin Sweeper Truck", "Directional boring equipment", "Pressure digger (54\" diameter, 20'' depth)"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Two dedicated service departments (electrical and transportation)", "\"What we install, we maintain\" philosophy with emergency repair coverage", "MSHA-certified technicians for mining and pit environments", "Four-year electrical apprenticeship program through NNMIEC", "Owner-operated vac and sweeper truck rental fleet"], "facts_used": ["Headquartered in Albuquerque, NM -> /about", "Operates across NM, CO, TX, AZ, CA, WY -> /about", "In business for over 40 years -> /about", "Provides electrical construction, testing, and service -> /services", "Airfield lighting and NAVAID installation and maintenance -> /", "Roadway construction, lighting, signalization, ITS -> /", "Transmission and distribution up to 115kV -> /services", "Directional boring and vertical drilling -> /services", "Vacuum excavation and potholing -> /services", "Electrical testing: infrared, arc flash, power quality -> /services", "Two service departments (electrical and DOT-transportation) -> /services", "Vac and sweeper truck rentals (Sterling LT9500, International 4300 Elgin) -> /services", "MSHA certifications for mine and pit work -> /about", "Family-oriented culture, NNMIEC apprenticeship program -> /about", "Projects: Bear Canyon Pedestrian Bridge, Montano Railrunner Station -> /services", "Member of NNMIEC, NMUCA, ABCNM, ACNM -> /about"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Bixby Electric, Inc. is a New Mexico Corporation engaged in electrical construction, testing, and service.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='bixby-electric-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Black Timber Furniture Company operates from a showroom in Four Corners, just outside Bozeman, Montana. Founded by veteran Todd Fullerton, the business has been handcrafting furniture for 13 years, building a reputation on traditional American values and a commitment to local, chemical-free materials.

The shop produces custom solid-wood pieces ranging from live-edge tables and farmhouse beds to Murphy beds and commercial-grade furniture. Each item is built using traditional woodworking techniques, with clients involved in selecting wood species — such as alder, red and white oak, black walnut, maple, cherry, and reclaimed barn wood — as well as finishes, hardware, and upholstery options.

The company serves both residential and commercial clients. Its portfolio includes furnishings for private homes, hotels, resorts, lodges, banks, corporate offices, and universities across Montana and the wider United States.

Fullerton’s veteran ownership informs a service model centered on integrity and heirloom quality. By sourcing regionally and avoiding synthetic finishes, Black Timber aims to deliver furniture that lasts for generations while supporting local supply chains.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom solid wood furniture", "Live edge furniture", "Murphy beds", "Commercial furniture", "Custom furniture design", "Wood species selection (Alder, Oak, Walnut, Maple, Cherry, Reclaimed barn wood)", "Custom finishing", "Upholstery (leather, fabric)"], "industries": ["Residential", "Hospitality (hotels, resorts, lodges)", "Commercial office", "Education (universities)", "Financial (banks)"], "materials": ["Alder", "Red Oak", "White Oak", "Black Walnut", "Maple", "Cherry", "Reclaimed Barn Wood"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Local, chemical-free material sourcing", "Full custom design collaboration (wood, finish, hardware, upholstery)", "Handcrafted using traditional woodworking techniques", "Veteran-owned, service rooted in traditional American values", "Heirloom-quality furniture built for generations"], "facts_used": ["Location: Bozeman, Montana -> db", "Owned by Veteran Todd Fullerton -> /", "13 years in business -> /", "Materials: Alder, Red Oak, White Oak, Black Walnut, Maple, Cherry, Reclaimed Barn Wood -> /", "Industries served: homes, hotels, banks, resorts, lodges, commercial offices, universities -> /", "Capabilities: Custom Solid Wood Furniture, Live Edge Furniture, Murphy Beds, Commercial Furniture -> db", "Showroom in Four Corners near Bozeman -> /", "Custom design collaboration (wood, finish, hardware, upholstery) -> /", "Traditional woodworking techniques -> /", "Chemical-free, local material sourcing -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We specialize in designing and creating hand-crafted, heritage-quality furniture using traditional techniques.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Veteran-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='black-timber-furniture-company' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='The business was established in 1999 and rebranded to its current name in 2019.

The shop produces custom apparel and promotional items entirely in-house, running screen-printing presses, embroidery machines, and direct-to-garment (DTG) printers under one roof. Additional capabilities include direct-to-film printing, leather patches, embroidered patches, 3D patches, PVC patches, puff embroidery, promotional products such as tumblers, bags and pens, signs and banners, and online merchandise stores for group ordering. Graphic design support and end-to-end fulfillment are also offered.

The company serves teams and leagues, schools and booster clubs, businesses and work crews, and churches and nonprofits, both locally and nationwide. Typical projects range from church retreat shirts and team uniforms to fundraiser merchandise, event signage and corporate branded gear.

Blazon emphasizes its community-focused mission, stating it is dedicated to bringing people together around companies, communities and causes through customized apparel. Practical differentiators include low minimum orders, a two-week standard turnaround with a one-week rush option, free delivery in the Greater Columbia area, and BBB A+ accreditation.', certifications=ARRAY['BBB A+ Accredited']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Screen printing", "Embroidery", "Direct-to-garment (DTG) printing", "Direct-to-film printing", "Leather patches", "Embroidered patches", "3D patches", "PVC patches", "Puff embroidery", "Promotional products sourcing", "Signs and banners", "Online merchandise stores", "Graphic design services", "End-to-end fulfillment"], "industries": ["Teams and leagues", "Schools and boosters", "Businesses and crews", "Churches and nonprofits"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "2 weeks standard, 1 week rush", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["In-house production: screen printing, embroidery and DTG under one roof", "Low minimum order quantities", "2-week standard turnaround, 1-week rush available", "Free delivery in Greater Columbia, SC area", "Family-owned and operated with BBB A+ accreditation"], "facts_used": ["Company name: Blazon Apparel + Print -> db", "Location: Gaston, South Carolina -> db, /about-us", "Established in 1999, rebranded to Blazon in 2019 -> /about-us", "Family-owned and operated -> /about-us", "In-house production: screen printing, embroidery, DTG under one roof -> /", "Capabilities: screen printing, embroidery, DTG, direct-to-film, leather patches, embroidered patches, 3D patches, PVC patches, puff embroidery -> /about-us", "Promotional products: tumblers, bags, pens -> /", "Signs and banners -> /", "Online merchandise stores for groups -> /", "Graphic design services -> /about-us", "End-to-end fulfillment -> /", "Industries served: teams and leagues, schools and boosters, businesses and crews, churches and nonprofits -> /", "Turnaround: 2 weeks standard, 1 week rush -> /", "Low minimums -> /", "Free delivery in Greater Columbia, SC area -> /about-us", "BBB A+ Accredited -> /", "Brands printed on: Bella + Canvas, Richardson, Next Level, Gildan, Nike, Under Armour, Champion -> /about-us", "Showroom in Gaston, SC -> /about-us", "Virtual consultations available -> /about-us", "Serving local and nationwide customers -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Printed in-house Presses, embroidery & DTG under one roof", "founded_year": "1999", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "Low minimums", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='blazon-apparel-print' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Blount Fine Foods is headquartered in Warren, Rhode Island, and traces its roots to 1880 when Eddie B. Blount started an oyster company on the coast of West Barrington. The business remains family-owned and operated through five generations, with F. Nelson Blount transforming it into a clam enterprise in Warren during the 1940s and Ted Blount diversifying into value-added seafood items like clam chowder in the 1980s.

Today the company manufactures premium fresh prepared foods — soups, chowders, sides, entrees, mac & cheese, and comfort meals — using kettle-cooking methods at a large plant built in Fall River, Massachusetts, in the 2000s. Its products are distributed to grocery stores, club stores, and restaurants across all 50 states, serving both retail and food-service channels.

Blount supplies food companies, finer dining establishments, and national retail chains, with its food-service and hot-to-go lines producing soups for recognizable brands. The company also operates its own Clam Shack line, drawing on New England seafood heritage.

Blount emphasizes simple, pronounceable ingredient lists and a blend of tradition and innovation. It holds several food safety certifications, supports community nonprofits through food donations, and maintains a family-oriented culture with employee benefits such as free meals and incentive programs.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Prepared foods manufacturing", "Product development", "Kettle cooking", "Food service supply", "Retail distribution", "Marketing and brand development"], "industries": ["Food manufacturing", "Food service", "Retail grocery", "Club stores", "Restaurants", "Fine dining"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Family-owned and operated for five generations", "Simple, pronounceable ingredient lists", "Kettle-cooked soups and chowders", "Food safety certifications earned", "Community giving through food donations"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1880 by Eddie B. Blount in Barrington, RI -> /about-us", "Family-owned and operated -> /about-us", "Headquarters in Warren, Rhode Island -> db", "Manufactures prepared soups, chowders, sides, entrees, mac & cheese, meals -> /about-us, /", "Sells to grocery stores, club stores, restaurants in all 50 states -> /about-us", "Operates a large plant in Fall River, MA -> /about-us", "Uses kettle cooking process -> /about-us", "Emphasizes simple, pronounceable ingredient lists -> /about-us", "Holds food safety certifications -> /about-us", "Donates food to local nonprofits -> /about-us", "Five generations of family leadership -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We''re a family-owned and operated marketer, manufacturer, and developer of premium fresh prepared foods.", "founded_year": "1880", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHE